      "title": "Start here",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Read a Premiere edit\n\n**No Premiere plugin needed.** Nothing to install, nothing to download. This one takes an edit you exported out of Premiere and tells you what is inside it.\n\n**1.** On **Load Premiere Timeline**, click **Browse...** and pick `sample_timeline.xml`, which sits next to this file in the pack's `examples/` folder.\n\nTo use your own edit instead: in Premiere, select a sequence and choose **File > Export > Final Cut Pro XML**, then Browse to the file you just wrote.\n\n**2.** Press **Run**. Three text previews fill in. Read them top to bottom.\n\nThe sample edit points at video files that do not exist on your machine. That is fine and deliberate -- these three nodes only read the *edit*: the cuts, the names, the timings. Nothing opens a media file, so nothing can be missing."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
