      "title": "Doing the whole edit",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Every segment at once\n\n**Iterate Premiere Segments** is the same idea without the `index`. It fires once per segment, so everything downstream of it runs once per cut. No loop node, no batching, nothing to set up.\n\nHere it drives a text preview, so you get one preview box per clip. Put a real workflow after it instead and you have just processed an entire edit in a single Run.\n\nCareful with this one on a long edit -- a hundred cuts means a hundred runs of everything downstream."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
